From: Valerie Snyder <valsnyde@cisco.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:25:20 -0400
Subject: libclamav: Validate InstallShield file tables (#156)

An InstallShield header can declare a large file count without
providing the corresponding fixed-size records. The parser continued
advancing past the missing table for every declared entry, allowing a
small PE to consume a scanner worker for an extended period.

Validate the header and table offsets, and cap iteration to complete
records physically available in the header. Continue scanning a valid
record prefix before falling back to raw scans for malformed metadata.
Stop on mapping failures and consult the scan deadline while processing
records.

Validate header-relative name offsets and cabinet stream bounds before
using them, including when malformed trailing data resembles a record.

Reported by Nebula Security.

CLAM-3070

